{"text": "Filed on 7/18/2013 4:01:50 PM\n\nIN THE SUPERIOR COURT OF THE STATE OF ARIZONA, In and for the County of Cochise\n\nJUDGE: HONORABLE JAMES L CONLOGUE, MARY ELLEN DUNLAP, Clerk of the Superior Court\n\nDIVISION: FIVE by: JO TINNEY (7/18/2013 9:30:38 AM), Deputy Clerk\nCOURT REPORTER: AARON SCHLESINGER\nINTERPRETER: HEARING DATE: 07/16/2013\n\nSTATE OF ARIZONA,\nPlaintiff,\n\nCASE NO: S0200CR201200116\n\nMINUTE ENTRY: COURT TRIAL\nVS\nHEARING START TIME: 09:00 AM\nSEVERO ANTHONY TORRES, III HEARING END TIME: 10:36 AM\n\nDefendant.\n\nState represented by Roger Contreras, Deputy County Attorney\nDefendant present in person and by Clarence Jenkins, Deputy Public Defender\n\nLET THE RECORD REFLECT that prior to the proceedings State\u2019s Exhibits 1, 2a through 2v, 3, 4a through 4m, 5, 6, 7,\n8, 9, 10a through 10g and Defendant\u2019s Exhibits A through Z and A-1 through U1 were marked for identification for\npreparation to conduct a Jury Trial. The said exhibits were not used for the proceedings.\n\nLET THE RECORD REFLECT that the Defendant has waived his right to a Jury Trial and has agreed that the matter be\nsubmitted to the Court based upon certain records.\n\nMr. Contreras submitted State\u2019s Exhibits 1 and 2 to the clerk for marking. He stated that the copies of the documents\nhave also been provided to the Defense.\n\nMr. Jenkins advised the Court that he has objection to the Court considering State\u2019s Exhibit 2 until a final verdict by the\nCourt has been reached.\n\nThe Court will only consider State\u2019s Exhibit 1 at this time.\nMr. Contreras advised the Court as to a preliminary matter.\nMr. Jenkins requested that the Court take Under Advisement a ruling as to whether or not the Defendant is guilty until\nthe Defense has presented argument on the Motion to Dismiss and that the Defendant not be remanded into custody until\nafter the Motion to Dismiss has been presented for decision by the Court. He further requested that certain documents be\nsealed that are contained in the Court file.\n\nThe Court requested that Mr. Jenkins identify each document that he is requesting to be sealed.\n\nThe Court stated if there is a finding of guilt the Defendant will be taken into custody.\n\nPage 1 of 3",
